Subject: [PATCH] x86/kvm: take only wake-ups from what a host offers

A KVM guest reads which paravirtual features its host offers from a CPUID
leaf of the hypervisor's own range, and takes each one the answer names: a
clock the host keeps, steal time and the preempted flag that goes with it,
an EOI or a page fault the host completes, a TLB flush the guest skips for
a vCPU the host reports preempted. Each of those lets the host decide
something the guest then computes with, and the last lets it leave a stale
translation in place. In a TD the TDX module has no part in that leaf: the
guest's #VE handler asks the host, and the host answers what it likes.

This kernel now takes three of them and nothing else, whatever its host
offers and whatever it runs on: the hypercall that sends an IPI, the one
that kicks a halted vCPU and the one that asks the host to run a vCPU.
Each asks the host to wake or run a vCPU, which it can delay or refuse, as
it can any interrupt, and none hands it anything the guest goes on to use.
With steal time not taken, the kernel's own use of the third, which goes
by the host's word that a vCPU is preempted, stays off. It takes no hint
either. Every reader of a feature or a hint goes through the two functions
changed here, kvmclock's and the idle driver's among them.

A guest that is no TD takes the same, so that it differs from a TD by its
hardware and by nothing its kernel takes from its host.

Linux-Version: 6.18.49
---
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/kvm.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/kvm.c
@@ -895,14 +895,29 @@
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(kvm_para_available);
 
+/*
+ * A guest's host answers the leaf that offers these features. Of what a
+ * host offers there, this kernel takes only what can delay it and cannot
+ * change what it computes: the hypercall that sends an IPI, the one that
+ * kicks a halted vCPU, and the one that asks the host to run a vCPU. A
+ * clock the host keeps, steal time, an EOI or a page fault the host
+ * completes, a TLB flush left to the host for a vCPU it reports preempted:
+ * it takes none of them, whatever is offered, and no hint. Every reader of
+ * a feature or a hint comes here.
+ */
+#define KVM_FEATURES_TAKEN	(BIT(KVM_FEATURE_PV_SEND_IPI) | \
+				 BIT(KVM_FEATURE_PV_UNHALT) | \
+				 BIT(KVM_FEATURE_PV_SCHED_YIELD))
+
 unsigned int kvm_arch_para_features(void)
 {
-	return cpuid_eax(kvm_cpuid_base() | KVM_CPUID_FEATURES);
+	return cpuid_eax(kvm_cpuid_base() | KVM_CPUID_FEATURES) &
+	       KVM_FEATURES_TAKEN;
 }
 
 unsigned int kvm_arch_para_hints(void)
 {
-	return cpuid_edx(kvm_cpuid_base() | KVM_CPUID_FEATURES);
+	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(kvm_arch_para_hints);
 
